          "version": 6
        },
        "fields": {
          "notes": "Work identity follows the current GND work authority. The provisional Russian translation in the local Mysl volume and the exact German 1888 Naumann witness are represented as distinct expressions; no textual equivalence or translation quality is inferred. The authorial route admits only exact source-backed W II 6 / W II 7 regions and inscription layers, never whole-notebook work membership. D 21 / GSA 71/28 is explicitly the Götzen-Dämmerung print manuscript and is not assigned to Der Fall Wagner. The complete 26 June print manuscript and 16 July fair copy are lost; the one-leaf, two-canvas Basel object NL 200 : II, 1 is the sole surviving correction/addition fragment, not a complete manuscript. Nietzsche's changes and the later Köselitz/Lauterbach provenance notes remain distinct responsibility layers. The existing unlabelled 1888 Item and the nominal Zweite Auflage half of the same 1000-copy run are not presumed textually identical or different."
        },
